    "https://career5.successfactors.eu/career?career_ns=job_listing&company=S003974031P&navBarLevel=JOB_SEARCH&rcm_site_locale=nl_NL&career_job_req_id=24639": {
      "title": "Endowed Professor 'Rijnlands kapitalisme: kenmerken, voorwaarden en mogelijkheden'",
      "description": "Endowed Professor 'Rijnlands kapitalisme: kenmerken, voorwaarden en mogelijkheden' (24639) JavaScript is uitgeschakeld in de webbrowser. Schakel JavaScript in om optimaal te profiteren van deze site, en vernieuw de pagina vervolgens. Laden... Verdergaan naar primaire inhoud Endowed Professor 'Rijnlands kapitalisme: kenmerken, voorwaarden en mogelijkheden' (24639) Vacature ID 24639 - Gepubliceerd - Vacatures voor wetenschappelijk personeel - Tilburg School of Humanities and Digital Sciences  Afdrukvoorbeeld vacatureomschrijving Solliciteren Vacature opslaan Vacature naar een vriend sturen Terug naar lijst Tilburg University | Tilburg School of Humanities and Digital Sciences (TSHD) in cooperation with Tilburg School of Catholic Theology (TST) and Tilburg School of Economics and Management (TiSEM) is searching for a Endowed Professor ‘Rijnlands kapitalisme: kenmerken, voorwaarden en mogelijkheden’ (m/f/x, 0.2 FTE, 5 years) Tilburg University invites applications for the endowed chair Rijnlands kapitalisme: kenmerken, voorwaarden en mogelijkheden. The chair focuses on the Rhineland, or continental European, approach to capitalism and examines the contributions it can make to contemporary societal challenges. The chair creates space for both academic research and public dialogue on the organization of the economy and society. Key themes include the moral and philosophical foundations of economic activity, the institutional conditions for broad prosperity, and new forms of entrepreneurship, cooperation and social responsibility. The chair builds on a long-standing intellectual tradition at Tilburg University. From the university's early years onwards, scholars such as Martinus Cobbenhagen and Frans Weve reflected on the social responsibility of business and the relationship between economy and society. The chair connects this tradition to contemporary developments such as digitalisation, artificial intelligence, sustainability, economic inequality and democratic resilience. Research and public dialogue The endowed professor will develop an independent research agenda on Rhineland capitalism and related questions. Possible themes include: What are the moral, political and institutional preconditions and characteristics of the Rhineland model of capitalism, and how can it further be developed in response to contemporary societal challenges? Which institutional arrangements, governance models and forms of entrepreneurship contribute to broad prosperity, social cohesion and sustainable economic development? How can insights from philosophy, economics, theology and related disciplines be integrated to better understand the relationship between markets, public institutions and civil society? How can scientific knowledge contribute to public debate and provide actionable insights for businesses, governments and societal organizations seeking to develop more inclusive and resilient economic systems? An important part of the chair is its contribution to public debate. The endowed professor is expected to bring academic expertise into wider discussions about the economy, values and society, and to communicate complex questions in accessible ways. Public lectures, essays, dialogue sessions, media engagement and other forms of knowledge exchange may form part of this work. Education and academic leadership Education is part of the chair, including guest lectures, seminars and student supervision. Depending on the candidate's profile and available opportunities, a broader contribution to interdisciplinary education may also be developed. We are looking for someone who enjoys building connections: across disciplines, between academia and society, and between established research traditions and new ideas. Experience in supervising students and PhD candidates and in interdisciplinary collaboration is an advantage. Embedding The chair is hosted by the Department of Philosophy of Tilburg School of Humanities and Digital Sciences (TSHD) and works closely with the Tilburg School of Economics and Management (TiSEM) and the Tilburg School of Catholic Theology (TST). This interdisciplinary setting brings together economic, philosophical, ethical and theological perspectives. The chair connects with existing university initiatives, including REDES – Resilient Democratic Society, the Academic Workplace (Be)sturen op Brede Welvaart, and the Centre for Religion in the Public Sphere. The chair is a joint initiative of Tilburg University and Socires, an independent centre for societal issues and with a focus on what holds societies together and makes them liveable and sustainable.The chair is made possible in part through the support of the Stichting Katholiek Hoger Onderwijs (SKHO) and connects with the tradition of Catholic social thought that has long been part of Tilburg University's intellectual identity. Tilburg University and Socires aim not only to strengthen research and societal dialogue through this collaboration, but also to explore further opportunities for joint development in education and research. The appointment is 0.2 FTE (one day per week). Research, education, public engagement and the further development of the chair will be organized in proportion to the scope of the appointment. At the same time, the position is intended as a starting point from which, depending on the candidate, the development of the chair and available opportunities, further involvement in education and research may be explored. Who are we looking for? We are looking for a committed and intellectually curious scholar who can connect economics with philosophy, ethics, theology, political theory, economic history or a related field. You hold a PhD and have published in relevant national and international academic journals and have the academic foundation to develop your own research agenda further. We welcome candidates from a variety of academic backgrounds. A fully developed profile specifically in Rhineland capitalism is not a prerequisite. What matters is a strong intellectual affinity with the subject, the ambition to develop a distinctive research agenda, and the ability to create meaningful connections across disciplines and with societal practice. You are also experienced or interested in connecting academic knowledge to society, and vice versa. Therefore, a proven record of working with (or realistic plans to do so) business and the public debate is recommended. Knowledge of/ambition to working with other societal partners and governments or other forms of knowledge exchange is a plus. You recognize and value the intellectual tradition of Tilburg University and Socires, including their interest in social responsibility, broad prosperity and Catholic social thought. Working from the chair you should be willing to engage with this tradition seriously and critically. A good command of Dutch is a requirement for this position. This is important because of the chair's contribution to Dutch public debate and its close engagement with societal partners in the Netherlands. A good command of English is expected for international academic collaboration and publication. Knowledge of a second or third language is an advantage. What we offer The candidate will be appointed as an endowed professor at Tilburg University at 0.2 FTE for an appointment period of 5 years. The start date is negotiable. Tilburg University offers excellent employment conditions with attention to flexibility and (personal) development. We make clear agreements about career paths and offer all kinds of facilities and arrangements to maintain an optimal balance between work and private life. The university actively pursues a policy for inclusive and interdisciplinary teams in which diverse talents are recognized and valued. The regulations and employment conditions of Tilburg University apply to remuneration and other employment conditions, in accordance with the university job classification as Professor 2. The gross salary varies between €7,475 and €10,815 per month (full-time) based on the Full Professor 2 scale of the Collective Labor Agreement for Dutch Universities. University employees are entitled to a holiday allowance of 8%, an end-of-year bonus of 8.3% of the gross annual income, and 41 days of holiday per year (based on full-time employment). We reimburse the full costs for sustainable commuting: walking, cycling, public transport or transport with a fully electric car. Interested? We warmly invite you to apply. The endowed chair’s structure report as well as additional information can be obtained from prof. dr. Maureen Sie, M.M.S.K.Sie@tilburguniversity.edu . We request that you attach the following documents to your application: cover letter (in Dutch) CV official copy of your university degree a representative publication and publication list research proposal or research agenda contact information of at least two reference persons (including name, phone number, and email address). We only approach referees for candidates who go to the second selection round. Applications are expected no later than November 12, 2026, online only, via the link. The selection interviews will be held in the week of December 3rd. Over Tilburg University Tilburg University is dé universiteit voor mens- en maatschappijwetenschappen. Al sinds onze oprichting in 1927 zetten we ons in voor een rechtvaardige, inclusieve en duurzame samenleving. Met toonaangevend onderzoek en inspirerend onderwijs dragen wij bij aan duiding en waar mogelijk aan oplossingen voor actuele maatschappelijke vraagstukken, van klimaatverandering tot digitalisering Onze gemeenschap is persoonlijk, betrokken en kleinschalig. Op onze groene, compacte en levendige campus is ruimte voor ontmoeting, samenwerking én reflectie en persoonlijke groei. Lees meer over Tilburg University . Werken bij Tilburg University doe je tegen aantrekkelijke arbeidsvoorwaarden in een inclusief team. Hier krijg je volop kansen voor het versterken van je talenten en het ontwikkelen van een loopbaan. In een warme werksfeer waarin we hechten aan de waarden: curious, connected, caring en courageous. Over Tilburg School of Humanities and Digital Sciences (TSHD) Onderzoek en onderwijs aan de Tilburg School of Humanities and Digital Sciences (TSHD) richt zich op mens, technologie, cultuur en hun interacties in een globaliserende digitale samenleving. Vanuit het samenspel van onze disciplines, richt ons onderzoek en onderwijs zich op de ontwikkeling van kunstmatige intelligentie en interactieve technologieën, hun invloed op communicatie, cultuur en samenleving, en morele en existentiële uitdagingen die zich voordoen. De School of Humanities and Digital Sciences bestaat uit zes departementen: Cognition & Communicatie, Computational Cognitive Science, Intelligent Systems, Cultuurwetenschappen, Filosofie en het Tilburg Center of the Learning Sciences. Zowel onderzoekers als studenten worden aangemoedigd om discipline-overstijgend samen te werken. Met deze aanpak stimuleren we een manier van denken die rekening houdt met verschillende perspectieven en de uiteenlopende, soms tegenstrijdige behoeften en belangen van mensen en de samenleving. Bij TSHD koesteren we een cultuur van integriteit, vertrouwen, diversiteit en inclusie, en constructieve en kritische dialoog. Alle leden van onze gemeenschap worden erkend en gewaardeerd om hun unieke bijdrage. University College Tilburg, met haar interdisciplinaire Liberal Arts and Sciences programma, heeft een unieke positie binnen de faculteit. Deze samenwerking met andere faculteiten omvat ook de disciplines economie, rechten en sociale wetenschappen. Lees meer over de Tilburg School of Humanities and Digital Sciences (TSHD) . Sollicitatiecode Tilburg University hanteert de NVP-sollicitatiecode van de Nederlandse Vereniging voor Personeelsmanagement & Organisatieontwikkeling. Disclaimer De tekst in deze vacatureadvertentie is auteursrechtelijk beschermd eigendom van Tilburg University. Gebruik, verspreiding en verdere openbaarmaking van de advertentie zonder uitdrukkelijke toestemming van Tilburg University is niet toegestaan en dat geldt expliciet voor gebruik door werving- en selectiebureaus welke niet rechtstreeks handelen in opdracht van de Tilburg University. Reacties naar aanleiding van werving door niet-opdrachtnemers van Tilburg University worden niet in behandeling genomen. Solliciteren Vacature opslaan Vacature naar een vriend sturen Terug naar lijst Deze functie naar een vriend sturen   De functie is verstuurd naar Geef onderstaande informatie op Vacaturetitel: * E-mailadres van uw vriend: Bericht: Maximum aantal tekens: 1000 * Bevestig dat u geen robot bent: Verzenden Annuleren"
    },
    "https://career5.successfactors.eu/career?career_ns=job_listing&company=S003974031P&navBarLevel=JOB_SEARCH&rcm_site_locale=nl_NL&career_job_req_id=24621": {
      "title": "Junior Researcher Fostering Creativity in Multicultural Classrooms through Educational Robotics ai",
      "description": "Junior Researcher Fostering Creativity in Multicultural Classrooms through Educational Robotics ai (24621) JavaScript is uitgeschakeld in de webbrowser. Schakel JavaScript in om optimaal te profiteren van deze site, en vernieuw de pagina vervolgens. Laden... Verdergaan naar primaire inhoud Junior Researcher Fostering Creativity in Multicultural Classrooms through Educational Robotics ai (24621) Vacature ID 24621 - Gepubliceerd - Vacatures voor wetenschappelijk personeel - Tilburg School of Humanities and Digital Sciences  Afdrukvoorbeeld vacatureomschrijving Solliciteren Vacature opslaan Vacature naar een vriend sturen Terug naar lijst Tilburg University | Tilburg School of Humanities and Digital Sciences is looking for a Junior Researcher in Fostering Creativity in Multicultural Classrooms through Educational Robotics and AI Department: Culture Studies (DCU) Location: Tilburg Contract size: 0.6 fte (24 hours per week) Full-time gross monthly salary: €3706 – €4251 Contract duration: 18 months Intended start date: January 2027 The Department of Culture Studies at Tilburg School of Humanities and Digital Sciences, Tilburg University, is seeking a junior researcher for a new Erasmus+ project on fostering creativity in multicultural classrooms through educational robotics and AI . The junior researcher will support the research team in the coordination and implementation of the project. Are you interested in fostering inclusion in multicultural classrooms? Do you like to explore how AI technologies are used to enhance creativity in classrooms with students from diverse backgrounds? Are you eager to work in an international team and gain project management experience? Then this position suits you well! Your position The successful candidate will work on a project funded by Dutch National Agency Erasmus+ Cooperation partnerships in school education. The project includes partners from the Netherlands, Cyprus, Greece and Turkey. The project aims to strengthen teachers’ capacity to foster creativity as a core student competence through AI, educational robotics and culturally responsive pedagogy; to develop innovative and technology-enhanced resources; to test and validate these resources in multicultural secondary classrooms; and to promote their adoption through dissemination and policy recommendations at regional, national and EU levels. You will be responsible for assisting the project team at DCU for 18 months in the following activities: Conducting Research: tasks include conducting research and analyzing existing educational resources, consulting experts in the field, and supporting the development of skillsets and training materials for teachers. Supporting Dissemination: tasks include assisting the Project Coordinator in organizing an international seminar in the Netherlands, and delivering training sessions for participant teachers. Supporting Project Management: tasks include assisting the Project Coordinator with project management activities, such as recording the timely implementation of the project activities by all partners, maintaining an organized archive of project-communication and administrative documents. Role focus: Your primary responsibility will be to conduct and support research activities. Dissemination, project management, and general administrative responsibilities will remain with the Project Coordinator, with your role being to provide support and assistance in these areas as needed. Your profile Motivated researcher with a master’s degree in Culture Studies, Educational Sciences, Communication Sciences or a related field Demonstrated ability to conduct high-quality academic research , evidenced by relevant outputs such as theses, research projects and publications Interest in and willingness to develop project management skills , including supporting the planning and coordination of project activities and project meetings A collaborative team player, who enjoys working in a dynamic and interdisciplinary environment Commitment to research integrity and ethical research practices , including accuracy, transparency and responsible handling of research data and information Excellent command of English (minimum CEFR C1 level; C2 level preferred). Proficiency in Dutch is considered an asset. Our offer Tilburg University offers excellent benefits in a pleasant working environment: Employment of 0.6 fte (24 hours per week). Salary between €3706 and €4251 gross per month for full-time employment (UFO-profile Researcher 4, salary scale 10 step 0 till step 3). Tilburg University uses a neutral remuneration system based on relevant work experience. This is a vacancy for a temporary position in accordance with Article 2.3 paragraph 5 sub b CLA DU. You will be given a temporary contract for the duration of 18 months. Vacation pay of 8% and a year-end bonus of 8.3%. Over 8 weeks of vacation leave. Hybrid working with home working allowance Reimbursement sustainable commuting: walking, cycling, and public transport. Options model for additional leave, pension, a bicycle or personal training. Moving allowance (subject to conditions). 30% rule for international employees (if applicable). Pension through ABP. Ample training offer: personal development, leadership, education, research or language courses. Inclusive work culture: everyone welcome, equal opportunities. A green, inviting campus that’s easily accessible by public transport. For more information, please see our website and the CLA Dutch Universities . Want to know more? Would you like to know more before applying? Feel free to contact Dr. Irem Bezcioğlu-Göktolga at i.bezcioglu@tilburguniversity.edu For more information about the department, you may reach out to Head of the Department of Culture Studies, prof. Odile Heynders ( O.M.Heynders@tilburguniversity.edu ). Want to apply? We kindly invite you to apply by 20 October 2026 ; this can only be done online . Please include the following documents in your application: A one-page cover letter explaining how you meet the selection criteria for this position, drawing on examples from your academic, professional and/or personal experiences A curriculum vitae (CV) Contact details of two references The letter selection will take place by November 1, 2026. You will be notified as soon as possible thereafter. The first selection interviews will take place on 10 November 2026. The selection committee consists of: dr. Irem Bezcioğlu-Göktolga Prof dr. Kutlay Yağmur dr. Rian Aarts dr. Amy Hsiao You will ideally start working for Tilburg University in January 2027. Over Tilburg University Tilburg University is dé universiteit voor mens- en maatschappijwetenschappen. Al sinds onze oprichting in 1927 zetten we ons in voor een rechtvaardige, inclusieve en duurzame samenleving. Met toonaangevend onderzoek en inspirerend onderwijs dragen wij bij aan duiding en waar mogelijk aan oplossingen voor actuele maatschappelijke vraagstukken, van klimaatverandering tot digitalisering Onze gemeenschap is persoonlijk, betrokken en kleinschalig. Op onze groene, compacte en levendige campus is ruimte voor ontmoeting, samenwerking én reflectie en persoonlijke groei. Lees meer over Tilburg University . Werken bij Tilburg University doe je tegen aantrekkelijke arbeidsvoorwaarden in een inclusief team. Hier krijg je volop kansen voor het versterken van je talenten en het ontwikkelen van een loopbaan. In een warme werksfeer waarin we hechten aan de waarden: curious, connected, caring en courageous. Over Tilburg School of Humanities and Digital Sciences (TSHD) Onderzoek en onderwijs aan de Tilburg School of Humanities and Digital Sciences (TSHD) richt zich op mens, technologie, cultuur en hun interacties in een globaliserende digitale samenleving. Vanuit het samenspel van onze disciplines, richt ons onderzoek en onderwijs zich op de ontwikkeling van kunstmatige intelligentie en interactieve technologieën, hun invloed op communicatie, cultuur en samenleving, en morele en existentiële uitdagingen die zich voordoen. De School of Humanities and Digital Sciences bestaat uit zes departementen: Cognition & Communicatie, Computational Cognitive Science, Intelligent Systems, Cultuurwetenschappen, Filosofie en het Tilburg Center of the Learning Sciences. Zowel onderzoekers als studenten worden aangemoedigd om discipline-overstijgend samen te werken. Met deze aanpak stimuleren we een manier van denken die rekening houdt met verschillende perspectieven en de uiteenlopende, soms tegenstrijdige behoeften en belangen van mensen en de samenleving. Bij TSHD koesteren we een cultuur van integriteit, vertrouwen, diversiteit en inclusie, en constructieve en kritische dialoog. Alle leden van onze gemeenschap worden erkend en gewaardeerd om hun unieke bijdrage. University College Tilburg, met haar interdisciplinaire Liberal Arts and Sciences programma, heeft een unieke positie binnen de faculteit. Deze samenwerking met andere faculteiten omvat ook de disciplines economie, rechten en sociale wetenschappen. Lees meer over de Tilburg School of Humanities and Digital Sciences (TSHD) . Sollicitatiecode Tilburg University hanteert de NVP-sollicitatiecode van de Nederlandse Vereniging voor Personeelsmanagement & Organisatieontwikkeling. Disclaimer De tekst in deze vacatureadvertentie is auteursrechtelijk beschermd eigendom van Tilburg University. Gebruik, verspreiding en verdere openbaarmaking van de advertentie zonder uitdrukkelijke toestemming van Tilburg University is niet toegestaan en dat geldt expliciet voor gebruik door werving- en selectiebureaus welke niet rechtstreeks handelen in opdracht van de Tilburg University. Reacties naar aanleiding van werving door niet-opdrachtnemers van Tilburg University worden niet in behandeling genomen. Solliciteren Vacature opslaan Vacature naar een vriend sturen Terug naar lijst Deze functie naar een vriend sturen   De functie is verstuurd naar Geef onderstaande informatie op Vacaturetitel: * E